.TH REGRESS-STACK 1 "August 2026" "regress-stack" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
regress-stack \- configure and test Ubuntu OpenStack packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B regress-stack
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B regress-stack
configures Ubuntu OpenStack packages on a single node and runs regression
tests against the resulting environment.
.PP
Most setup and test operations require root privileges. Run
.B regress-stack COMMAND --help
for command-specific usage information.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "list-modules"
List all available OpenStack modules in dependency order.
.TP
.BI "packages " [TARGET]
Print the packages needed for all modules, or for the specified target.
The space-separated output can be passed directly to
.BR apt (8).
.RS
.TP
.B --no-tempest
Exclude Tempest-related packages, for example when using the Tempest snap.
.RE
.TP
.BI "plan " [TARGET]
Display the module execution order for all modules, or for the specified
target.
.TP
.B playground
Create a basic OpenStack playground with an Ubuntu image, network, flavor,
project, and user.
.TP
.BI "setup " [TARGET]
Configure all modules, or configure the dependency chain for the specified
target.
.TP
.B test
Discover and run the configured Tempest regression tests.
.RS
.TP
.BI "--concurrency " WORKERS
Set the number of test workers. The default is 1; the value
.B auto
uses one third of the available CPUs.
.TP
.BI "--retry-failed " COUNT
Retry failed tests up to
.I COUNT
times. The default is 0.
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show help for the command and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List the available modules:
.EX
regress-stack list-modules
.EE
.TP
Show the execution plan for Nova:
.EX
regress-stack plan nova
.EE
.TP
Install packages needed for Nova without Tempest packages:
.EX
sudo apt install $(regress-stack packages --no-tempest nova)
.EE
.TP
Configure the complete environment and run tests with four workers:
.EX
sudo regress-stack setup
sudo regress-stack test --concurrency 4 --retry-failed 1
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/user.rc
OpenStack credentials generated by the
.B playground
command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR tempest (1)
